From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:20:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [telepathy] Fix farstream callback lifetimes, DTMF and
 unhandled requests.

Farstream:
- The start-sending, stop-sending and src-pad-added handlers on each
  TfContent got the FarstreamChannel as user data and were never
  disconnected; only the TfChannel's were. Reference the contents and
  disconnect their handlers when they are removed and in the destructor.
- onStartSending() returned bool to a signal that returns gboolean, so
  the marshaller read an int whose upper bits weren't set.
- src-pad-added for video, or with audio output that failed to set up,
  passed a NULL bin to GStreamer.
- A NULL self was dereferenced in the very checks meant to catch it.
- Pad and peer references were leaked in onStopSending(),
  onSrcPadAddedContent() and removeBin(), and the destructor cleared
  mSHClosed instead of each handler id.

Channels:
- A conference that was invalidated cleared its children's parent ids
  but kept them in childCalls. Children deleted first could then no
  longer remove themselves, and the conference's destructor wrote to
  them after they were freed. Clear the list.
- DTMF sent tones.toInt(): "123" was sent as event 123, lower case
  letters were dropped, and the D-Bus timeout was set to 0. Map single
  keys to their event, and send longer strings with MultipleTones.
- CallChannelHandler created a new Hold or DTMF interface proxy on every
  hold() and sendDtmf(), kept until the call ended. Use the channel's.

Provider:
- handleChannels() never answered the channel dispatcher for accounts
  that aren't registered, which then waited for the D-Bus timeout.
- createConference() for SIP connected to a null request and returned
  true. Fail with an error like the other unsupported cases.
- The plugin's destructor dereferenced the client registrar even if
  initialize() never ran.

Add a unit test of the DTMF key mapping.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
